// The one world the cut-silence plugin implements.
//
// Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0, like `subordinate:plugin` itself, so a
// plugin author may copy this file along with the rest of the plugin.
//
// A plugin is one component, and a component has one world; cut-silence needs
// two entry points that live in two of the host's worlds:
//
//   - `analyze`, from `subordinate:plugin/analyzer`, which finds the silence;
//   - `run`, from `subordinate:plugin/command`, which cuts it out.
//
// So the world below is the union of the two: the same export signatures, drawn
// from the same interfaces, and `command-api` — the only way a plugin edits a
// project — imported once. Because the signatures and their types are the
// host's own, `plugin.wasm` instantiates against the host's `analyzer` bindings
// and its `command` bindings alike, and `plugin.toml` honestly declares both
// worlds.
//
// What is deliberately *not* imported is `subordinate:plugin/analysis-host`,
// the analyzer world's progress and cancellation channel. A component only
// instantiates when every import it declares is in the linker, and the host's
// `command` world links `command-api` alone; importing `analysis-host` here
// would make this component loadable as an analyzer but not as a command. The
// cost is that one `analyze` call reports no progress and cannot be cancelled
// before it returns, which is affordable only because this analyzer's work is
// bounded: it reads one audio file once. An analyzer that thinks for minutes
// should be its own component and import `analysis-host`.

package subordinate:cut-silence@0.1.0;

/// Silence detection and silence removal in one component.
world cut-silence {
    use subordinate:plugin/types@0.1.0.{error, media-id, project-id};
    use subordinate:plugin/analysis@0.1.0.{analysis-result};

    import subordinate:plugin/command-api@0.1.0;

    /// `subordinate:plugin/analyzer`'s export: finds the silent spans of one
    /// media item and reports them, in media time, without editing anything.
    export analyze: func(media: media-id, options: string) -> result<analysis-result, error>;

    /// `subordinate:plugin/command`'s export: removes the silence the analyzer
    /// found from the clips `args` names, rippling each track, as one undo step.
    export run: func(project: project-id, args: string) -> result<string, error>;
}
